Wait — there's a subtle behavioral change in the non-dir arm: previously `split_parent(destination_path)?` then `validate_name(name)?` — with my restructure, validate_name moved after the match, so the non-dir arm still validates (just after the match, covers both arms) ✓ and the dir arm also validates the source basename ✓. But note the non-dir arm previously returned errors from split_parent before resolve(parent) — same order now-ish (parent resolution inside the arm) ✓.

One subtle issue: the dir arm uses the source's base name. validate_name rejects "." and ".." — a source file can never be named "." or ".." (validate_name at creation). split_parent(source_path)?.1 — for source_path = "/" the earlier resolve would have errored (rm on root? mv source root → RootOperation before). ✓.

Another subtle issue: the dir arm with source basename containing multibyte chars — validate_name enforces UTF-8 bytes ≤ 31 ✓ (any valid child name passes).

